%U A383111 3081,3588,4034,4697,5245,6091,6809,7833,8747,10067,11198,12829,14260,16266,18070,20550,22797,25838,28635,32350,35781,40353
%N A383111 Number of integer partitions of n having more than one permutation with all distinct run-lengths.
%C A383111 From _Alper Ferudun_, Jul 22 2026: (Start)
%C A383111 A partition is Look-and-Say exactly when its distinct-part multiplicities m_i admit pairwise-disjoint strict partitions P_i of m_i (A239455). A valid word gives such a family from its run lengths. Conversely, choose such a family minimizing K = Sum_i |P_i|. If P_i = {r_1 < ... < r_k} and k > 1 + (K-k), then K <= 2k-2. The k values r_1,...,r_k and the k-1 sums r_j+r_k (1 <= j < k) are 2k-1 distinct integers because each sum exceeds r_k and the sums differ with j. Exactly K values are used globally and all r_1,...,r_k are used, so some sum r_j+r_k is unused. Replacing r_j,r_k by this sum preserves m_i, strictness and disjointness but lowers K, a contradiction. Thus |P_i| <= 1 + Sum_{h != i}|P_h| for every i. By the standard gap criterion, the block labels can be ordered with unequal neighbors; assigning these lengths yields a valid word. This proves the conjectured converse in A239455.
%C A383111 If a valid word with more than one run equaled its reversal, its first and last runs would have the same length, impossible. Hence each nonconstant partition counted by A239455 has at least two valid words. Constant partitions have exactly one and are counted by A000005. Therefore a(n) = A239455(n) - A000005(n) for n >= 1.
%C A383111 (End)
%H A383111 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A383111/b383111.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..250</a>
%H A383111 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A383111/a383111.cpp.txt">C++ program used to compute a(n) for n <= 250</a>
%F A383111 For n >= 1, a(n) = A239455(n) - A000005(n). - _Alper Ferudun_, Jul 22 2026
%e A383111 The partition (2,1,1) has two permutations with all distinct run-lengths: (1,1,2), (2,1,1), so it is counted under a(4).
%e A383111 The a(4) = 1 through a(9) = 13 partitions:
%e A383111   (211)  (221)   (411)    (322)     (332)      (441)
%e A383111          (311)   (3111)   (331)     (422)      (522)
%e A383111          (2111)  (21111)  (511)     (611)      (711)
%e A383111                           (2221)    (5111)     (3222)
%e A383111                           (4111)    (22211)    (6111)
%e A383111                           (22111)   (41111)    (22221)
%e A383111                           (31111)   (221111)   (33111)
%e A383111                           (211111)  (311111)   (51111)
%e A383111                                     (2111111)  (222111)
%e A383111                                                (411111)
%e A383111                                                (2211111)
%e A383111                                                (3111111)
%e A383111                                                (21111111)
%t A383111 Table[Length[Select[IntegerPartitions[n], Length[Select[Permutations[#], UnsameQ@@Length/@Split[#]&]]>1&]],{n,0,15}]
%o A383111 (Python)
%o A383111 from itertools import groupby
%o A383111 from sympy.utilities.iterables import partitions, multiset_permutations
%o A383111 def a(n):
%o A383111     c = 0
%o A383111     for p in partitions(n):
%o A383111         cp = 0
%o A383111         for mp in multiset_permutations(p):
%o A383111             passes, run_lengths = True, set()
%o A383111             for k, g in groupby(mp):
%o A383111                 rl = len(list(g))
%o A383111                 if rl in run_lengths:
%o A383111                     passes = False
%o A383111                     break
%o A383111                 run_lengths.add(rl)
%o A383111             if passes:
%o A383111                 cp += 1
%o A383111             if cp > 1:
%o A383111                 c += 1
%o A383111                 break
%o A383111     return c
%o A383111 print([a(n) for n in range(21)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 02 2025
%o A383111 (C++) // See Links.
%Y A383111 For a unique choice we have A000005, ranks A000961.
%Y A383111 For at least one choice we have A239455, ranks A351294, conjugate A381432.
%Y A383111 For no choices we have A351293, ranks A351295, conjugate A381433.
%Y A383111 The complement is A351293 + A000005, ranks too dense.
%Y A383111 For equal instead of distinct run-lengths we have A383090, ranks A383089.
%Y A383111 These partitions are ranked by A383113 = positions of terms > 1 in A382771.
%Y A383111 Cf. A047966, A098859, A130091, A353837, A100471, A100881, A100882, A100883
%Y A383111 A000041 counts integer partitions, strict A000009.
%Y A383111 A008284 counts partitions by length, strict A008289.
%Y A383111 A329738 counts compositions with equal run-lengths, ranks A353744.
%Y A383111 Cf. A047993, A329739, A381541, A381636, A381717, A382857, A382915, A383013, A383092, A383094, A383097.
